Build users on illumos (solnix 0009).

Without this the daemon runs every build as root on illumos, whatever
build-users-group says: useBuildUsers() is true only on Linux and macOS.
Enable it under __sun as on macOS (a non-empty build-users-group, daemon
running as root); the rest of the path (getgrnam/getpwnam, the userpool
lock, setgroups/setgid/setuid, chown of the build dir and the pty, the
output uid check and lchown back) is POSIX and unchanged.

killUser() needs a change too. It forks, setuid(uid), kill(-1, SIGKILL).
illumos kill(-1) also signals the CALLER (uts/common/syscall/sigqueue.c
sigqkill -> sigsendset(P_ALL, P_MYID); dotoprocs skips only SSYS and
init). Linux excludes it, and nix passes macOS's kill a third argument
false so it does there. So the child dies of its
own SIGKILL, wait() returns a signal status and killUser throws "cannot
kill processes for uid", failing every build: startBuilder calls
killSandbox before each one. Measured on dixi (solnix 26.11, root):
  su nobody -c 'sleep 300 & kill -9 -1; echo SURVIVED'
  -> "ksh93: 886: Killed", rc 265: the caller died, its sleeper too;
  root's session survived (after setuid to a non-root uid the process
  has only basic privileges, so hasprocperm limits it to that uid).
On __sun use sigsendset(POP_DIFF, P_UID uid, P_PID self): every process
whose effective uid is uid, except this one. EPERM/ESRCH (none left)
still end the loop. P_UID, not P_ALL: it holds even if the child kept a
privilege. Gap: a setuid program the builder ran (euid 0, ruid uid) is
not matched; Linux's kill(-1) would kill it.

--- a/src/libstore/unix/user-lock.cc	2025-06-24 10:08:50.000000000 -0400
+++ b/src/libstore/unix/user-lock.cc	2026-10-28 15:45:46.608198657 -0400
@@ -196,7 +196,7 @@
     #if __linux__
     static bool b = (settings.buildUsersGroup != "" || settings.autoAllocateUids) && isRootUser();
     return b;
-    #elif __APPLE__
+    #elif __APPLE__ || __sun
     static bool b = settings.buildUsersGroup != "" && isRootUser();
     return b;
     #else
--- a/src/libutil/unix/processes.cc	2025-06-24 10:08:50.000000000 -0400
+++ b/src/libutil/unix/processes.cc	2026-10-28 15:45:46.608734798 -0400
@@ -22,6 +22,11 @@
 # include <sys/syscall.h>
 #endif
 
+#ifdef __sun
+# include <signal.h>
+# include <sys/procset.h>
+#endif
+
 #ifdef __linux__
 # include <sys/prctl.h>
 # include <sys/mman.h>
@@ -144,6 +149,14 @@
                which means "follow POSIX", which we don't want here
                  */
             if (syscall(SYS_kill, -1, SIGKILL, false) == 0) break;
+#elif defined(__sun)
+            /* illumos kill(-1) signals the caller too (sigqkill: P_ALL
+               minus system processes and init only), so this child died
+               of its own SIGKILL and wait() reported failure. Send to
+               every process of uid except ourselves. */
+            procset_t set;
+            setprocset(&set, POP_DIFF, P_UID, uid, P_PID, getpid());
+            if (sigsendset(&set, SIGKILL) == 0) break;
 #else
             if (kill(-1, SIGKILL) == 0) break;
 #endif
